===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*terkʷ-}}
The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|torch}}, {{m|enm|torche|t=large candle; lighted stick; (''figurative'') sunbeam}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=torch(e|pos=n|id=MED46345}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|torche}}, {{m|fro|torque|t=torch; bundle of (twisted) straw}} (modern {{cog|fr|torche}}); further etymology uncertain, probably from {{der|en|la-vul|*torca|t=coiled object}} (referring to a torch made from twisted plant fibres dipped in a flammable substance such as pitch), from {{der|en|la|torqua}}, a variant of {{m|la|torquis|t=collar of twisted metal, torque; wreath}}, from {{m|la|torqueō|t=to twist, wind}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*terkʷ-|t=to spin; to turn}}.<ref name="OED">Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=5976979929|date=March 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref>

{{senseno|en|common mullein|uc=1|pos=false}} ({{taxfmt|Verbascum thapsus|species}}) is either due to the plant’s spike of yellow flowers, or because its leaves and stalks were used to make torches ''(noun {{senseno|en|burning stick|pos=false}})''. {{senseno|en|pass on the torch|uc=1|pos=false}} (“precious cause, etc., which needs to be protected and transmitted to others”) is derived from {{cog|la|[[lampada]] [[trādere]]}}, from {{cog|grc|[[λᾰμπᾰ́ς|λᾰμπᾰ́δᾰ]] [[πᾰρᾰδῐ́δωμῐ|πᾰρᾰδιδόναι]]|t=to hand over the torch}}, a reference to the torch race held at various festivals such as the {{w|Panathenaic Games}} in Ancient Greece,<ref name="OED"/> which involved a relay where a torch was passed from one runner to another.

The {{glossary|verb}} is derived from the noun.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''v.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=7456606527|date=July 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref>

