===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=noun|:inh|enm:tost|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|tost}}, from the verb {{m|enm|tosten}} (see below).

{{senseno|en|to which a salutation is made|cap=1|pos=false}} is according to the ''{{w|Oxford English Dictionary}}'' a figurative application of {{senseno|en|Q6128|pos=false}} dating to 1674. It began as an epithet for ''a lady being supposed to flavour a [[bumper]] like a spiced toast placed in that drink.'' (In this context, a ''bumper'' is a drinking vessel filled to the brim.)

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

