===Etymology 2===
{{etymon|en|id=verb|:inh|enm:tosten|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|tosten}}, from {{der|en|fro|toster||to roast, grill}}, from {{der|en|la-lat|tostō,|-āre}}, frequentative of {{m|la|torreō||to burn, grill}} from its perfect passive participle {{m|la|tostus||grilled, burnt}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{senseid|en|cook lightly}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cook]] lightly by [[brown#Verb|browning]] [[by means of]] [[direct]] [[exposure]] to a [[fire]] or other [[heat]] [[source]].
#: {{ux|en|We used to enjoy '''toasting''' marshmallows around the campfire.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|specifically}} To [[cook]] lightly by [[brown#Verb|browning]] under a [[grill#Noun|grill]] or in a [[toaster]]; to [[grill#Verb|grill]].
#: {{ux|en|Top with cheese and '''toast''' under the grill for a few minutes.}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To engage in a [[salutation]], often with raising of the drinking {{l|en|vessel|id=mineral container}}, while drinking an [[alcoholic]] [[beverage]] in honor of someone or something.
#: {{ux|en|We '''toasted''' the happy couple many times over the course of the evening.}}
#: {{ux|en|You all have achieved so much together thus far, so I think that deserves a toast! Let's '''toast'''!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[warm]] [[thoroughly]].
#: {{ux|en|I '''toasted''' my feet by the fire.}}
# {{lb|en|music|slang|Jamaica}} To [[perform]] an [[extemporaneous]] [[narrative]] [[poem]] or [[rap]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Richard James Burgess|title=The History of Music Production|publisher=Oxford University Press|isbn=9780199357161|page=168|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ZeISDAAAQBAJ&pg=PA168&dq=%22version%22+sound+system&hl=&cd=12&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22version%22%20sound%20system&f=false|text='''Toasting''' over a record does more than change the way that record is perceived by the audience: it creates a new piece of music with joint creative authorship, although the law does not support this characterization.}}

